{"jazz":{"id":"43fda4d8-81c8-4cf1-b25f-c87c94beff66","word":"jazz","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"musical art form","tags":["masculine"],"word":"jazz"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the (in)tangible substance that goes into the makeup of a thing; unspecified thing(s)","tags":["feminine"],"word":"porcariada"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the (in)tangible substance that goes into the makeup of a thing; unspecified thing(s)","tags":["feminine"],"word":"coisarada"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"of excellent quality, the genuine article","tags":["masculine"],"word":"suprassumo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"nonsense","tags":["feminine"],"word":"besteira"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"You dare to bring your jazz songs into my house!","ref":"1927, Samson Raphaelson, Alfred A. Cohn, The Jazz Singer, spoken by Jakie Rabinowitz (Al Jolson):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,27]],"id":"37b1d035-0492-4d52-b4ef-74230f4a328a"},{"text":"Of later composers of Jewish musical plays we mention Joseph Rumshinksy (born in Wilna in 1879), who gained popularity in New York. His music is based upon folk motives and influenced by \"Jazz\" rhythms and melodic curves","ref":"1929, Abraham Zevi Idelsohn, Jewish Music: Its Historical Development, page 454:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[188,192]],"id":"ed072f60-54ba-4c0b-8574-8f7494790119"},{"text":"You all look out now, here I come, everybody step aside, I’m gonna show you where from! I'm gonna blow in this horn and make you know that jazz is the king and let it be so!","ref":"1946, Milton “Mezz” Mezzrow, Bernard Wolfe, “Not too Far Tangent”, in Really the Blues, New York, N.Y.: Random House, book 1 (1899–1923: A Nothin’ but a Child), page 30:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[139,143]],"id":"babdd098-0e8c-4ee3-9390-6e196b3eb002"},{"text":"You see, the kids, they listen to the rap music which gives them the brain damage. With their hippin', and the hoppin', and the bippin', and the boppin', so they don't know what the jazz…is all about! You see, jazz is like the Jello Pudding Pop—no, actually, it's more like Kodak film—no, actually, jazz is like the New Coke: it'll be around forever, heh heh.","ref":"1995 April 30, Mike Reiss, Al Jean, “'Round Springfield”, in The Simpsons, season 6, episode 22, spoken by Bill Cosby (Dan Castellaneta):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[182,186],[210,214],[299,303]],"id":"9b88d88e-5bb3-444a-be2b-1ceb13e85fd6"}],"topics":["entertainment","lifestyle","music"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Musical genres"],"links":[["music","music"],["African American","African American"],["blues","blues"],["blue note","blue note"],["syncopation","syncopation"],["swing","swing"],["call and response","call and response"],["polyrhythm","polyrhythm"],["improvisation","improvisation"]],"raw_glosses":["(music) A musical art form rooted in West African cultural and musical expression and in the African American blues tradition, with diverse influences over time, commonly characterized by blue notes, syncopation, swing, call and response, polyrhythms and improvisation."],"glosses":["A musical art form rooted in West African cultural and musical expression and in the African American blues tradition, with diverse influences over time, commonly characterized by blue notes, syncopation, swing, call and response, polyrhythms and improvisation."],"tags":["uncountable","usually"],"id":"869ec2f1-0d19-4da4-9057-4f9ddb0c8cb0"},{"examples":[{"text":"“You want something zippy there. Something with a bit of jazz to it!”","ref":"1923 May 17, P[elham] G[renville] Wodehouse, “(please specify the page)”, in The Inimitable Jeeves, Harmondsworth, Middlesex [London]: Penguin Books, published 1979, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[57,61]],"id":"f2d423c5-30ab-4764-bdb6-aa5b4988e98d"},{"text":"He loves the risk. The danger. He loves the jazz.","ref":"1983, Frank Lupo, Stephen J. Cannell, “Mexican Slayride”, in The A-Team, season 1, episode 1, spoken by B. A. Baracus (Mr. T):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[44,48]],"id":"75c61ece-da69-4675-b779-c38e953d810f"}],"links":[["Energy","energy#English"],["excitement","excitement"],["excitability","excitability"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(figurative) Energy, excitement, excitability."],"glosses":["Energy, excitement, excitability."],"tags":["figuratively","uncountable","usually"],"id":"5b5ccc7f-3f44-4736-90f6-1a4aa2e44e2f"},{"examples":[{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"and all that jazz","bold_text_offsets":[[13,17]],"type":"example","id":"fba1f058-80b2-41fe-a8c3-74d2ba8fbac5"},{"text":"What is all this jazz lying around?","bold_text_offsets":[[17,21]],"type":"example","id":"69db81fe-e8e3-4597-a9a1-8c76516b13e8"},{"text":"I'm just going down to the shops and jazz.","bold_text_offsets":[[37,41]],"type":"example","id":"6b1c96ac-9d81-4c4a-95c1-435e9612d4e8"},{"text":"Dad, I want to be a jock. All a jock needs is some hep patter and a real gone image. Now, they just don't teach that jazz in college.","ref":"1975, Garry Marshall et al., “Richie's Flip Side”, in Happy Days, season 2, episode 21, spoken by Richie Cunningham (Ron Howard):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[117,121]],"id":"e775a470-e8b2-46ac-ae29-ff3fe8b119b0"}],"senseid":["en:stuff"],"synonyms":[{"word":"stuff"},{"word":"Sorted by number of Google hits","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"widget","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"hickey","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"gizmo","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"thingy","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"gimmick","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"thingie","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"jigger","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"gismo","source":"Thesaurus:thingy"},{"word":"gubbins","source":"The